// `@FR-G-Next` / `@FR-G-Delegate` — an advance runs ONE slice, from the resume point.  So
// the statements a generator runs before it suspends run once per ACTIVATION, never once
// per advance.  The
// resume point of a suspended `yield from` is inside the delegation; it is not the top of
// the statements that led there.
//
// `--native` lowers a generator to a state machine, one state per segment.  A `yield from`
// segment took ONE state and had to stay in it to keep pulling, so every advance re-entered
// the state at its top — where the segment's `pre` sits.  The prefix therefore ran again on
// every advance the delegation served: a counter incremented three times for one increment,
// a `v += [7]` landing three elements in a vector the program reads afterwards.  The
// produced SEQUENCE is identical under either lowering, so no value of the generator itself
// said so and the differential oracle read green.  `ForLoopLazy` already answered the
// identical question with a dedicated once-only setup state; the cure is that answer.
//
// Two more faces of the same segment's bookkeeping travel with it, and they are native
// COMPILE failures rather than wrong values.  They live in
// `a-delegation-beside-a-loop-compiles.loft` and not here ON PURPOSE: a generator that does
// not compile ends the whole run before any assertion is reached, so holding both faces in
// one file would leave the five value cells below UNSCORED against the very tree they were
// written to catch.  One channel per guard.
//
// Axes this file MOVES:  where the prefix sits (before the delegation, between two of them,
//                        after the last one, none at all), what the prefix IS (one
//                        statement, three of them, a loop, an append to a caller-visible
//                        vector), what PRECEDES the delegation (nothing, a plain `yield`,
//                        another delegation), and how much the consumer takes (all of it,
//                        one value).
// Axes it HOLDS FIXED:   the delegate is a plain two-yield generator throughout — its own
//                        shape was never the question, and the cell below measures that its
//                        prologue already ran exactly once.  A LOOP before the delegation is
//                        the other file's axis, because there it is an exit-channel question
//                        and here it would be an unscorable one.  The yielded TYPE is
//                        `tests/coroutine_matrix.rs`'s X5 column.
//
// @falsified-at: 2026-09-25 by hand, against the tree before the cure (e40409f5f),
//   `--native` only — the interpreter is the values oracle and passes every cell on BOTH
//   trees, which is the whole shape of the defect:
//   test_the_prefix_of_a_delegation_runs_once        pro=3, expected 1
//   test_every_statement_of_the_prefix_runs_once     11/100 -> 33/300
//   test_a_prefix_that_appends_appends_once          len=3, expected 1
//   test_a_prefix_loop_runs_once                     pro=9, expected 3
//   test_a_prefix_between_two_delegations_runs_once  pro=3, expected 1
//   test_the_prefix_runs_once_per_activation_...     pro=6, expected 2
//   Each of those five was scored on its OWN run with `main` cut down to that cell, because
//   the first failed assertion ends the program and only one of the five would otherwise
//   speak; the four control cells were scored the same way and PASS on the control tree.
//   CHANNEL: assert — both backends run and compute, and the values disagree.  Not exit:
//   nothing crashes.  Not leak: nothing leaked either way, which is part of why this
//   survived — the sub-generator frame is NOT re-minted per advance (the cell below
//   measures that), only the caller's own statements re-ran.
//   ARMED: no instrument — `--interpret` is the values oracle and a plain `--native` run
//   reads every cell.  Clean under `LOFT_POISON=1 LOFT_STRICT_STORES=1`.
//   WITNESS: `test_the_prefix_of_a_delegation_runs_once` — one counter, incremented once by
//   the program's own control flow, read after the generator is drained.
//   HOLDS: the six control cells at the end.  A prefix before a plain `yield`, a prefix
//   before a lazily-lowered loop, a delegation with no prefix at all and two adjacent
//   delegations all answered identically before the cure, and must keep doing so — they are
//   what says the once-only state was added to the delegation and nowhere else.
//   Two of those six also BOUND the defect: a delegation under an `if` arm and one inside a
//   loop body answer correctly on the control tree, because a block, loop or `if` containing
//   a yield sends the whole generator to the EAGER collector and the state machine is never
//   reached.  So the defect is exactly a `yield from` at the generator's TOP LEVEL, and the
//   cells written expecting a PASS are what established that.
//
// Cross-backend; `main` runs every cell so the leak gate reads the file.

struct GdLog { n: integer, m: integer }

fn gd_two() -> iterator<integer> { yield 1; yield 2; }

fn gd_counting(lg: reference<GdLog>) -> iterator<integer> { lg.m = lg.m + 1; yield 8; yield 9; }

fn prefix_before(lg: reference<GdLog>) -> iterator<integer> {
  lg.n = lg.n + 1;
  yield from gd_two();
  yield 3;
}

fn prefix_of_three(lg: reference<GdLog>) -> iterator<integer> {
  lg.n = lg.n + 1;
  lg.n = lg.n + 10;
  lg.m = lg.m + 100;
  yield from gd_two();
}

fn prefix_appends(acc: vector<integer>) -> iterator<integer> {
  acc += [7];
  yield from gd_two();
  yield 3;
}

fn prefix_is_a_loop(lg: reference<GdLog>) -> iterator<integer> {
  for i in 0..3 { lg.n = lg.n + 1 + i * 0; }
  yield from gd_two();
}

fn prefix_between_two(lg: reference<GdLog>) -> iterator<integer> {
  yield from gd_two();
  lg.n = lg.n + 1;
  yield from gd_two();
}

// --- controls: shapes that already agreed, and must keep agreeing ---

fn prefix_before_a_plain_yield(lg: reference<GdLog>) -> iterator<integer> {
  lg.n = lg.n + 1;
  yield 1; yield 2; yield 3;
}

fn prefix_before_a_lazy_loop(lg: reference<GdLog>) -> iterator<integer> {
  lg.n = lg.n + 1;
  for i in 1..4 { yield i; }
}

fn delegation_under_a_branch(lg: reference<GdLog>, on: boolean) -> iterator<integer> {
  lg.n = lg.n + 1;
  if on { yield from gd_two(); }
  yield 3;
}

fn delegation_in_a_loop_body(lg: reference<GdLog>) -> iterator<integer> {
  lg.n = lg.n + 1;
  for _ in 0..2 { yield from gd_two(); }
}

fn delegation_with_no_prefix() -> iterator<integer> {
  yield from gd_two();
  yield 3;
}

fn two_adjacent_delegations() -> iterator<integer> {
  yield from gd_two();
  yield from gd_two();
}

fn test_the_prefix_of_a_delegation_runs_once() {
  // The statement that needs no rule reference: one increment in the program's control
  // flow, four advances (1, 2, 3, done), and the counter reads 1.
  lg = GdLog { n: 0, m: 0 };
  t = 0;
  for x in prefix_before(lg) { t = t + x; }
  assert(lg.n == 1, "the prefix runs once per activation: {lg.n}");
  assert(t == 6, "and the sequence is unchanged: {t}");
}

fn test_every_statement_of_the_prefix_runs_once() {
  lg = GdLog { n: 0, m: 0 };
  t = 0;
  for x in prefix_of_three(lg) { t = t + x; }
  assert(lg.n == 11, "both prefix statements run once: {lg.n}");
  assert(lg.m == 100, "the third one too: {lg.m}");
  assert(t == 3, "sequence 1,2: {t}");
}

fn test_a_prefix_that_appends_appends_once() {
  // The damaging face: a container the program reads after the generator is drained.
  acc: vector<integer> = [];
  t = 0;
  for x in prefix_appends(acc) { t = t + x; }
  assert(len(acc) == 1, "one append, one element: {len(acc)}");
  assert(acc[0] == 7, "and it is the value appended: {acc[0]}");
  assert(t == 6, "sequence 1,2,3: {t}");
}

fn test_a_prefix_loop_runs_once() {
  lg = GdLog { n: 0, m: 0 };
  t = 0;
  for x in prefix_is_a_loop(lg) { t = t + x; }
  assert(lg.n == 3, "a loop in the prefix runs once, not once per advance: {lg.n}");
  assert(t == 3, "sequence 1,2: {t}");
}

fn test_a_prefix_between_two_delegations_runs_once() {
  lg = GdLog { n: 0, m: 0 };
  t = 0;
  for x in prefix_between_two(lg) { t = t + x; }
  assert(lg.n == 1, "a prefix between two delegations runs once: {lg.n}");
  assert(t == 6, "sequence 1,2,1,2: {t}");
}

fn test_the_delegates_own_prologue_still_runs_once() {
  // Measured BEFORE the cure and already correct: the sub-generator frame is minted once,
  // not re-minted per advance.  Here so the cure is not read as having fixed that too.
  lg = GdLog { n: 0, m: 0 };
  t = 0;
  for x in gd_counting(lg) { t = t + x; }
  assert(lg.m == 1, "the delegate's own prologue runs once: {lg.m}");
  assert(t == 17, "sequence 8,9: {t}");
}

fn test_the_shapes_that_already_ran_the_prefix_once() {
  // Controls.  A prefix before a plain `yield` and before a lazily-lowered loop each sit in
  // a segment that already had somewhere to put a once-only statement.
  a = GdLog { n: 0, m: 0 };
  ta = 0;
  for x in prefix_before_a_plain_yield(a) { ta = ta + x; }
  assert(a.n == 1, "prefix before a plain yield: {a.n}");
  assert(ta == 6, "sequence 1,2,3: {ta}");

  b = GdLog { n: 0, m: 0 };
  tb = 0;
  for x in prefix_before_a_lazy_loop(b) { tb = tb + x; }
  assert(b.n == 1, "prefix before a lazy loop: {b.n}");
  assert(tb == 6, "sequence 1,2,3: {tb}");
}

fn test_the_delegation_shapes_that_already_compiled() {
  // Controls for the two compile faces: with no earlier segment, and with an adjacent one,
  // the segment index and the state index agreed and the field was found.
  ta = 0;
  for x in delegation_with_no_prefix() { ta = ta + x; }
  assert(ta == 6, "delegation then a yield: {ta}");

  tb = 0;
  for x in two_adjacent_delegations() { tb = tb + x; }
  assert(tb == 6, "two adjacent delegations: {tb}");
}

fn test_the_prefix_runs_once_per_activation_not_once_per_program() {
  // The rule says once per ACTIVATION, and this is the cell that tests that word: the same
  // generator is activated twice over one shared counter.  `scripts/matrix_axes.py` named the
  // axis (A9, evaluation count) on the otherwise-finished file — every other cell here
  // activates exactly once, so "once" and "once per activation" were indistinguishable.
  lg = GdLog { n: 0, m: 0 };
  t = 0;
  for x in prefix_before(lg) { t = t + x; }
  for x in prefix_before(lg) { t = t + x; }
  assert(lg.n == 2, "two activations run the prefix twice, not more: {lg.n}");
  assert(t == 12, "and each yields 1,2,3: {t}");
}

fn test_a_delegation_under_a_branch_or_in_a_loop_keeps_its_prefix_once() {
  // Over-reach controls, and they are what bounds the defect: BOTH of these answered
  // correctly on the control tree.  A block, loop or `if` containing a yield sends the whole
  // generator to the EAGER collector (`collect_segments`), whose factory runs the body once
  // up front — so the state machine, and with it the question this file is about, is never
  // reached.  The defect is exactly a `yield from` at the generator's TOP LEVEL.
  a = GdLog { n: 0, m: 0 };
  ta = 0;
  for x in delegation_under_a_branch(a, true) { ta = ta + x; }
  assert(a.n == 1 && ta == 6, "branch taken: {a.n} / {ta}");

  b = GdLog { n: 0, m: 0 };
  tb = 0;
  for x in delegation_under_a_branch(b, false) { tb = tb + x; }
  assert(b.n == 1 && tb == 3, "branch not taken: {b.n} / {tb}");

  c = GdLog { n: 0, m: 0 };
  tc = 0;
  for x in delegation_in_a_loop_body(c) { tc = tc + x; }
  assert(c.n == 1 && tc == 6, "delegation in a loop body: {c.n} / {tc}");
}

fn test_a_consumer_that_stops_early_runs_the_prefix_once() {
  // One advance always ran the prefix exactly once — the divergence began at the second.
  // The cell that reads right on both trees, kept because it bounds the defect.
  lg = GdLog { n: 0, m: 0 };
  first = 0;
  for x in prefix_before(lg) { first = x; break; }
  assert(first == 1, "the first value arrives: {first}");
  assert(lg.n == 1, "and the prefix ran once: {lg.n}");
}

fn main() {
  test_the_prefix_of_a_delegation_runs_once();
  test_every_statement_of_the_prefix_runs_once();
  test_a_prefix_that_appends_appends_once();
  test_a_prefix_loop_runs_once();
  test_a_prefix_between_two_delegations_runs_once();
  test_the_prefix_runs_once_per_activation_not_once_per_program();
  test_a_delegation_under_a_branch_or_in_a_loop_keeps_its_prefix_once();
  test_the_delegates_own_prologue_still_runs_once();
  test_the_shapes_that_already_ran_the_prefix_once();
  test_the_delegation_shapes_that_already_compiled();
  test_a_consumer_that_stops_early_runs_the_prefix_once();
}
